  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "3802-root",
    "title": "AKU Faculty Named Among World's Top 2% Scientists",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "The faculty, alumnus from Pakistan and Kenya are leading researchers in their fields",
    "media": [],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Twenty-seven faculty members and one alumnus from the Aga Khan University have been named in the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "World's Top 2% Scientists List for 2024",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://elsevier.digitalcommonsdata.com/datasets/btchxktzyw/8",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " by Stanford University. Of these twenty-seven individuals, fifteen faculty members are also alumni. This notable achievement highlights the University's significant contributions to global research and its commitment to academic excellence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The annual list, a globally respected benchmark, identifies leading researchers across a broad range of disciplines. The rankings are based on standardized citation data from Elsevier's Scopus database, which measures the impact of scientists' work through academic citations and the quality of the peer-reviewed journals in which their research is published."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\"These rankings reflect not only the incredible talent housed within AKU but also the University's steadfast dedication to fostering an environment of excellence,\" said Dr Salim Virani, Vice Provost, Research at AKU. \"We have consistently invested in state-of-the-art research facilities and fostered collaborations with world-leading institutions to encourage the pursuit of quality and innovation in our research.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Twenty-five faculty members were recognized for their single-year research impact in 2024. This latest ranking is an increase from the 19 faculty who were listed in 2023. The recognition underscores AKU's role as a leading research institution in the developing world, with its faculty driving impactful discoveries in several research fields."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The recognised faculty members, hailing from Pakistan and Kenya, are distinguished across two categories:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1. Recognized for Single Recent Year Impact",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This list highlights researchers based on their citations during the most recent calendar year, reflecting a high current impact:"
